 jleo@khjon:~$ git status                                                    
  fatal: not a git repository (or any parent up to mount point /home)         
  Stopping at filesystem boundary (GIT_DISCOVERY_ACROSS_FILESYSTEM not set).  
                                                                              

● That's just because you're not inside the project folder — git only knows
  about the repo when you're in (or under) /home/jleo/my-website. Your home
  directory itself (~) isn't a git repo.
 
  Fix:
  cd ~/my-website
  git status
  
  As long as your terminal prompt shows you're inside my-website (or any
  folder under it), git commands will work. If you cd back out to ~ or
  anywhere else, you'll get that same "not a git repository" error again —
  that's git correctly telling you "there's nothing to track here."

